        "name": "Melaka heritage town",
        "description": "A UNESCO trading port of red Dutch buildings, Jonker Street and river cruises.",
        "details": "Melaka has the Dutch Stadthuys, A Famosa fort ruins and Jonker Street, with a night market on weekends. The river cruise passes murals. Peranakan food, such as laksa and chicken rice balls, is a speciality. It is two hours from Kuala Lumpur.",
        "interests": [
