        "name": "Cameron Highlands tea plantations and Mossy Forest",
        "description": "Cool hill-station scenery with tea estates, strawberry farms and a cloud forest walk.",
        "details": "The Cameron Highlands sit at 1,500 metres, with tea plantations such as BOH and the Mossy Forest, a boardwalk through moss-draped trees. Temperatures are cool, so bring a jumper. Tea rooms serve scones. Roads wind steeply from the plains.",
